# The map's tiles (MapTiler). Optional: without it every address field still works and the map is
# simply not drawn.
#
# This one reaches the browser, and that is the design: tiles are fetched by the page, so no key
# can stay behind. Restrict it in MapTiler with "Allowed HTTP Origins" — the browser sends Origin
# and a page cannot forge it.
#
# It is NOT the key the API geocodes with. That one is server-side, in apps/api/.env, restricted by
# user-agent instead. Two keys, because the two restrictions cannot both apply to one: a server
# sends no Origin and is refused the moment any origin is listed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_TILE_KEY=

# The real-time channel's origin: where the browser opens its socket to the API — the one connection
# that skips the BFF, since a route handler cannot hold a WebSocket open. It carries only a single-use
# ticket, never the session. Here the API itself; in production behind one domain, the web's own
# origin, with the proxy sending /api/socket.io to the API. Inlined at build, like every NEXT_PUBLIC_
# value; unset, the channel stays shut and every page still works by reading again.
# See docs/repo/realtime.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME_URL=http://localhost:3001

# A shop's slug the landing page links to as "Ver uma loja de exemplo". Optional and server-only:
# unset, the landing offers no example rather than a link to a shop this deployment may not have.
EXAMPLE_STORE_SLUG=

# Which deployment this is. Optional and server-only: unset is production, unmarked. `homolog` puts
# the flag "AMBIENTE DE HOMOLOGAÇÃO" over every page and keeps search engines out.
APP_ENVIRONMENT=

# The platform's own host — the host alone, no https:// and no path. Optional and server-only: set, a
# request by it never asks whose host it is; unset, every host is looked up in the table of shop
# hosts (kept in memory, read from the API once a minute), which is what development and the e2e do.
# A shop's own domain is told from the platform's by the host of the request (BEELINK-283).
WEB_DOMAIN=

# Beelink's own GA4 measurement ID (G-…), for the landing's own visits. Optional and server-only:
# unset — here, in the e2e of a shop, in homologation — the landing asks nothing, draws no cookie
# notice and writes no cookie. Set, a visitor is asked (BEELINK-319), and one who says yes has
# Google's script loaded on the landing, the sign-in and the sign-up — never without that yes, and
# on no other page (BEELINK-320). Production's value is set in production's environment alone,
# never here.
SITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
